      "claim_id": "c1",
      "claim_text": "OpenAI reports that internal benchmarks show 40-80% better cache utilization on Responses than Chat Completions because Responses persists raw chain-of-thought tokens between turns via `previous_response_id` or encrypted reasoning items.",
      "claim_status": "measured"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "claim_text": "Compaction and other context-engineering steps can break the cache, so context engineering and prompt caching are presented as competing objectives that must be balanced.",
      "claim_status": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "claim_text": "A common failure mode is an overgrown tool set that creates tool-choice ambiguity; the guide recommends keeping the tool surface minimal and using `allowed_tools` to prune per request without busting the cache.",
      "claim_status": "asserted"
    }
  ],
